From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: vi_layer: Keep a unit step for crops off the chroma grid

For subsampled formats the fetch window is aligned to the chroma grid:
an odd crop width loses a column, an odd crop x moves the start one
pixel left and adds a phase. The scaler step was computed from that
aligned size, so a 1:1 plane with an odd crop was resampled by e.g.
1022/1023 across its whole width.

Compute the step from the crop, as the vendor driver does
(de_vsu_calc_scaler_para), and keep the aligned size for the fetch
window. A 1:1 plane now maps every pixel 1:1; only a column or row the
aligned window drops repeats its neighbour.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_vi_layer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_vi_layer.c
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 	struct sun8i_mixer *mixer = engine_to_sun8i_mixer(scrtc->engine);
 	const struct drm_format_info *format = state->fb->format;
 	u32 src_w, src_h, dst_w, dst_h;
+	u32 crop_w, crop_h;
 	u32 outsize, insize;
 	u32 hphase, vphase;
 	u32 hn = 0, hm = 0;
@@ -86,8 +87,10 @@
 
 	ch_base = sun8i_channel_base(layer);
 
-	src_w = drm_rect_width(&state->src) >> 16;
-	src_h = drm_rect_height(&state->src) >> 16;
+	crop_w = drm_rect_width(&state->src);
+	crop_h = drm_rect_height(&state->src);
+	src_w = crop_w >> 16;
+	src_h = crop_h >> 16;
 	dst_w = drm_rect_width(&state->dst);
 	dst_h = drm_rect_height(&state->dst);
 
@@ -156,6 +159,7 @@
 			vm = src_h;
 			vn = (u32)ability * dst_h / 100;
 			src_h = vn;
+			crop_h = vn << 16;
 		}
 
 		if (subsampled)
@@ -168,10 +172,15 @@
 			hm = src_w;
 			hn = scanline;
 			src_w = hn;
+			crop_w = hn << 16;
 		}
 
-		hscale = (src_w << 16) / dst_w;
-		vscale = (src_h << 16) / dst_h;
+		/*
+		 * The step follows the crop, not the fetch size aligned to
+		 * the chroma grid above, or a 1:1 plane gets resampled.
+		 */
+		hscale = crop_w / dst_w;
+		vscale = crop_h / dst_h;
 
 		sun8i_vi_scaler_setup(layer, src_w, src_h, dst_w, dst_h,
 				      hscale, vscale, hphase, vphase, format,
